=== Maintaining a Project
tag::concept[]

(((maintaining a project)))
In addition to contributing, Nora also has to **maintain** the SketchSpark project. This means she is responsible for reviewing, testing, and integrating the work that Sam, Priya, and Marcus send her way.

==== Working in Topic Branches
tag::procedure[]

(((branches, topic)))
When Nora receives a contribution—whether it's an icon set from Priya or a fix from Marcus—she never merges it directly into `main`. Instead, she creates a temporary **topic branch** to evaluate it.

[source,bash]
----
$ git checkout -b review/marcus-token-fix main
----

This allows her to test the changes in isolation. If something is broken, she can tweak it or discard the branch entirely without ever affecting the stable project history.

==== Integrating Work
tag::concept[]

(((integrating work)))
Once Nora is happy with the work in a topic branch, she has to decide how to integrate it. She has two main choices:

*   **Merging:** The simplest way. It creates a "merge commit" that clearly shows when the feature was brought in. This is Nora's default choice for large features from Sam or Priya.
*   **Rebasing/Cherry-Picking:** If Nora wants to keep a perfectly linear history, she can rebase the work or "cherry-pick" a single commit. This is great for small fixes from external contributors like Marcus, making it look like the fix was always part of the project's natural progression.

==== Tagging Milestones
tag::procedure[]

(((tags)))
When SketchSpark reaches a major milestone—like the first time the AI model successfully generates a mobile layout—Nora marks it with a **tag**.

[source,bash]
----
$ git tag -a v0.5-alpha -m "First end-to-end AI pipeline working"
$ git push origin v0.5-alpha
----

This tag acts as a permanent bookmark. If the team ever needs to go back and see exactly what the "Alpha" version looked like, they can do so in seconds.

==== Generating Reports
tag::reference[]

(((git commands, shortlog)))
Before the team's weekly design sync, Nora uses the `git shortlog` command to see a summary of everyone's contributions:

[source,bash]
----
$ git shortlog --no-merges main --since="1 week ago"
Nora UX (3):
      [Research: Persona] Update early-adopter goals
      [Research: Product] Refine vision statement

Sam UI (2):
      [Design: Results] Add initial grid layout
      [Design: Tokens] Update primary blue palette
----

This gives Nora a clean, human-readable list of everything that has happened in the SketchSpark project over the last week.

==== Summary
tag::overview[]

Maintaining a project is about more than just managing files; it’s about protecting the **integrity** of the design. By using topic branches, thoughtful integration, and clear tagging, Nora ensures that SketchSpark remains organized, stable, and ready for its next big launch.
